# Removes the trailing balanced bracket pair, so only the name remains.
# e.g. $myMethod(456,myvar) ==> $myMethod ,  $do('a b') ==> $do ,  $do(a(b)) ==> $do
# IMPORTANT: keeps the args out so a parsed method name is never executed with parameters.
# Works for ANY bracket content (quotes, spaces, nesting) — scans from the end, balancing.

Calculate name as pString

# only act if the string ends in a closing bracket
If mid(name,len(name),1)=')'
	Calculate level as 0
	Calculate pos as len(name)
	While pos>0
		If mid(name,pos,1)=')'
			Calculate level as level+1
		Else If mid(name,pos,1)='('
			Calculate level as level-1
			If level=0 ## matching opening bracket found
				Calculate name as mid(name,1,pos-1) ## cut from here to the end
				Break to end of loop
			End If
		End If
		Calculate pos as pos-1
	End While
End If

Quit method name